    the Software is not operated as a commercial service or business.

Private Use does not include operating a publicly accessible server, public game service, matchmaking service, or other instance intended to provide access to the Software or a Modified Version to the general public.

“Commercial Use” means use of the Software for the purpose of obtaining monetary compensation, generating revenue, promoting a commercial product or service, providing a commercial service, or otherwise using the Software in connection with a commercial enterprise.

“Modified Version” means any work based upon or incorporating the Software or a substantial portion of the Software that has been changed, adapted, translated, or otherwise modified.

“Distribute” means providing, transmitting, publishing, releasing, selling, sublicensing, or otherwise making a copy of the Software or a Modified Version available to another person or entity.

“Publicly Hosted” means operating or making the Software or a Modified Version accessible over a network to members of the public or to an unrestricted group of third parties.

